          "code": "INIT_DISPLAY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1774891813992",
          "id": "1774888351111",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774888351112_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_BATCH_PLANNED_QUANTITY_DEVIATIONS.$output}}, extract the following fields for each record:\n- DeviationCategory\n- DeviationCategoryCode\n- PercentDeviation\n- QuickMetrics\n- YieldImpact\n\nRender the output in this exact order:\n1. One plain-text summary paragraph\n2. One multiRecordWidget\n3. The Yield Impact legend text in a smaller font than the summary and widget text\n\nDo not return raw JSON, explanations, or instructions.\n\nBefore the multiRecordWidget output, render one plain-text summary paragraph:\n- A generated production supervisor or manufacturing engineer style summary, less than 60 words. Base it only on the records shown. Highlight what requires attention, including high-impact planned quantity deviations, affected ingredient/product/resource categories, batch counts, percent deviation, and actionable guidance to validate planning inputs, review category details, and address variance drivers.\n\nImportant summary formatting rules:\n- Do not use `description`.\n- Do not use `subtitle`.\n- Do not put the summary inside the multiRecordWidget properties.\n- The summary must be plain text outside the widget.\n- The summary must appear immediately above the multiRecordWidget.\n- The summary must be exactly one paragraph.\n\nAfter the multiRecordWidget output, render the Yield Impact legend outside the widget using small text exactly as shown:\n\n<small><br/>* Low <=10%, Medium >10% and <=20%, High >20%</small>\n\nImportant legend formatting rules:\n- Do not include the Yield Impact legend in the multiRecordWidget Subject, description, subtitle, columns, rows, badges, or any other widget property.\n- The Yield Impact legend must be plain text outside the widget.\n- The Yield Impact legend must appear immediately below the multiRecordWidget.\n- Render the Yield Impact legend in a slightly smaller font size than the summary and widget text.\n- The visible rendered text must appear exactly as:\n  * Low <=10%, Medium >10% and <=20%, High >20%\n\nDo not use phrases like \"the table\", \"below table\", \"displayed data\", \"below data\", or \"shown above\".\n\nGenerate a dynamic multiRecordWidget Subject:\n- If all records have PercentDeviation equal to 0, null, or blank, or YieldImpact is No Variance, set Subject as \"No Planned Quantity Deviations\".\n- If any record has non-zero PercentDeviation or YieldImpact other than No Variance, set Subject as \"Planned Quantity Deviations Requiring Attention\".\n- The Subject must be concise, specific, and aligned with the actual deviation status.\n\nDisplay the results using a multiRecordWidget with the following columns and exact order:\n1. DeviationCategory → Category\n2. PercentDeviation → Deviation\n3. QuickMetrics → Quick Metrics\n4. YieldImpact → Yield Impact*\n\nEnsure:\n- Each row represents one record from the source data.\n- Return the plain-text summary first, then the multiRecordWidget, then the Yield Impact legend.\n- Set the multiRecordWidget Subject property using the dynamic Subject rule above.\n- Do not set a multiRecordWidget description.\n- Do not set a multiRecordWidget subtitle.\n- Display PercentDeviation values with a % suffix, for example 89.55%, 23.57%, or -1568.68%.\n- Display YieldImpact as badgeText.\n- Set Priority strictly from YieldImpact:\n  - High → alert\n  - Medium → warning\n  - Low → medium\n  - No Variance → success\n- Preserve the exact column order specified above.\n- #ACTION For each row with DeviationCategoryCode, generate an actionable insight with ora.Agent(\"DeviationCategoryCode\") only when PercentDeviation is not null and non-zero. The actionText is View Details, and priority is false."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Planned Deviation Summary"
