          "code": "INGREDIENT_VARIANCE",
          "id": "1775924609154",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775924609155_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "From {{$context.$nodes.GET_PLANNED_BATCH_INGREDIENT_VARIANCE.$output}}, extract the following fields for each record:\n- Process\n- Recipe\n- Batch\n- Ingredient\n- BatchPlannedIngredient\n- BatchActualIngredient\n- Deviation\n- PercentDeviation\n- UomCode\n- WorkDefinitionId\n- WorkOrderStatusCode\n- WorkOrderStatusMeaning\n- WorkDefinitionItemNumber\n\nGenerate a description in less than 100 words using a production supervisor or manufacturing engineer tone. Base it only on the records shown. Highlight what requires attention, including ingredient planned quantity variance, affected process/recipe/batch/ingredient, recipe quantity versus batch actual quantity, deviation, percent deviation, and UOM. Provide actionable guidance to validate batch consumption, check ingredient issue records, review recipe setup, and investigate variance drivers. Do not use phrases like \"the table\", \"below table\", \"displayed data\", \"below data\", or \"shown above\".\n\nGenerate a dynamic multiRecordWidget Subject:\n- If all records have `Deviation` and `PercentDeviation` equal to 0, null, or blank, set Subject as \"No Ingredient Planned Quantity Deviations\".\n- If any record has non-zero `Deviation` or non-zero `PercentDeviation`, set Subject as \"Ingredient Planned Quantity Deviations Requiring Attention\".\n- The Subject must be concise, specific, and aligned with the actual deviation status.\n\nDisplay the results using a multiRecordWidget with the following columns and exact order:\n\n1. Process → Process\n2. Recipe → Recipe\n3. Batch → Batch\n4. Ingredient → Ingredient\n5. BatchPlannedIngredient with UomCode → Recipe Quantity\n6. BatchActualIngredient with UomCode → Batch Planned Quantity\n7. Deviation → Deviation\n8. PercentDeviation → Deviation Percentage\n9. WorkOrderStatusMeaning → Batch Status\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nROW ACTION\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFor each row, check the value of the 'WorkOrderStatusMeaning' attribute.\nIf 'WorkOrderStatusMeaning' is equal to 'UNRELEASED' or 'RELEASED', include the following action in that same row:\n\n- 'title':'SyncBatch'\n- 'followUpCommand': 'ora.Agent({\"command\": \"SyncBatch\",\"OrgId\":{{$context.$variables.organizationId}},\"FromDate\":\"01-01-1900\",\"ToDate\":<ToDate>,\"WorkDefinitionId\":<WorkDefinitionId>,\"ItemCategoryId\":<ItemCategoryId>,\"FromItemNumber\":<FromItemNumber>,\"ToItemNumber\":<ToItemNumber>,\"IncludeAllWO\":\"N\",\"FromWorkOrder\":<FromWorkOrder>,\"ToWorkOrder\":<ToWorkOrder>})'\n- 'actionText': 'Synchronize'\n- 'shortDescription': 'View the conformance check result details of the specified batch.'\n\nUse the 'OrganizationId' → {{$context.$variables.organizationId}}\n'ToDate' → Use {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} + 1 day in YYYY-MM-DD format\n'WorkDefinitionId' → Use WorkDefinitionId of the current row\n'ItemCategoryId' → null\n'FromItemNumber' → Use WorkDefinitionItemNumber of the current row\n'ToItemNumber' → Use WorkDefinitionItemNumber of the current row\n'IncludeAllWO' → Send 'N'\n'FromWorkOrder' → Use Batch of the current row\n'ToWorkOrder' → Use Batch of the current row\n\nEnsure:\n- Each row represents one record from the source data.\n- Only the multiRecordWidget is returned as the output.\n- Set the multiRecordWidget Subject property using the dynamic Subject rule above.\n- Set the generated description as the multiRecordWidget `description` property.\n- The `description` must render below the Subject and above the column headers and records.\n- Do not render the description as footer text, trailing text, an extra row, or content after the records.\n- Do not display raw JSON, explanations, or instructions.\n- Do not include `UomCode` as a separate column.\n- Display `BatchPlannedIngredient` values with `UomCode` appended, for example `100 KG`.\n- Display `BatchActualIngredient` values with `UomCode` appended, for example `95 KG`.\n- Display PercentDeviation values with a `%` suffix, for example `12.5%`, `0%`, or `-8.75%`.\n- Preserve the exact column order specified above."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
