 the value of the 'WorkOrderStatusMeaning' attribute.\nIf 'WorkOrderStatusMeaning' is equal to 'UNRELEASED' or 'RELEASED', include the following action in that same row:\n\n- 'title':'SyncBatch'\n- 'followUpCommand': 'ora.Agent({\"command\": \"SyncBatch\",\"OrgId\":{{$context.$variables.organizationId}},\"FromDate\":\"01-01-1900\",\"ToDate\":<ToDate>,\"WorkDefinitionId\":<WorkDefinitionId>,\"ItemCategoryId\":<ItemCategoryId>,\"FromItemNumber\":<FromItemNumber>,\"ToItemNumber\":<ToItemNumber>,\"IncludeAllWO\":\"N\",\"FromWorkOrder\":<FromWorkOrder>,\"ToWorkOrder\":<ToWorkOrder>})'\n- 'actionText': 'Synchronize'\n- 'shortDescription': 'View the conformance check result details of the specified batch.'\n\nUse the 'OrganizationId' → {{$context.$variables.organizationId}}\n'ToDate' → Use {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} + 1 day in YYYY-MM-DD format\n'WorkDefinitionId' → Use WorkDefinitionId of the current row\n'ItemCategoryId' → null\n'FromItemNumber' → Use WorkDefinitionItemNumber of the current row\n'ToItemNumber' → Use WorkDefinitionItemNumber of the current row\n'IncludeAllWO' → Send 'N'\n'FromWorkOrder' → Use Batch of the current row\n'ToWorkOrder' → Use Batch of the current row\n\nEnsure:\n- Each row represents one record from the source data.\n- Only the multiRecordWidget is returned as the output.\n- Set the multiRecordWidget Subject property using the dynamic Subject rule above.\n- Set the generated description as the multiRecordWidget `description` property.\n- The `description` must render below the Subject and above the column headers and records.\n- Do not render the description as footer text, trailing text, an extra row, or content after the records.\n- Do not display raw JSON, explanations, or instructions.\n- Do not include `UomCode` as a separate column.\n- Display `BatchPlannedOutput` values with `UomCode` appended, for example `100 KG`.\n- Display `BatchActualOutput` values with `UomCode` appended, for example `95 KG`.\n- Display PercentDeviation values with a `%` suffix, for example `12.5%`, `0%`, or `-8.75%`.\n- Preserve the exact column order specified above."
